<title>JAPAN: Japan May aluminium imports up 1.6 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan May aluminium imports up 1.6 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports totalled 241,098 tonnes in May, up 1.6 percent from 237,414 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry statistics released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   May 97	April 97    May 96</p>
<p>  Total	  241,098     266,133     237,414</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p>  Russia	  45,746	76,664	55,834</p>
<p>  Brazil	  33,093	23,245	15,572</p>
<p>  Australia     29,022	6,716	 43,285</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refined aluminium in the first four months of 1997 were 1,195,745 tonnes, up from 1,061,329 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
